Kubernetes won. That is a fact about industry adoption, not automatically a
fact about your three servers.

This is the second of two posts about what I would use *instead of* [the k3s
platform kit](/blog/k3s-platform-kit/). The other end of that spectrum is
[three FreeBSD boxes and no orchestrator at
all](/blog/three-freebsd-boxes-instead-of-k3s/). Docker Swarm is the middle,
and the one I think is genuinely under-rated.

::: note
**Part 5 of 7 of [Where to start with self-hosting](/blog/running-things-on-your-own-hardware/)**, a series about self-hosting a platform, and about whether you should.

Previous: [Three FreeBSD boxes instead of a k3s cluster](/blog/three-freebsd-boxes-instead-of-k3s/)

Next: [What a game world server actually needs](/blog/what-a-game-world-server-needs/)
:::

